{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521276-removing-flaws","id":1521276,"title":"Removing flaws","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-23T13:06:50-07:00","id":1521276,"title":"Removing flaws","content":"I'm not sure there is any rule about that (couldn't find in M20, at least), but ia it possible to get rid of flaws?<br /> <br /> Do it costs xp?<br /> <br /> There are many physical and mental flaws, some wuite severe and other more light, like hard of seeing, which could be easily corrected with cirurgy.<br /> <br /> And what about magick? Life or Mind could easily heal many flaws. How do you rule that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T14:23:40-07:00","id":1521283,"title":"","content":"Logically it makes sense for you to take some of these flaws, however I think it would be unbalanced to permit that, I mean, you can take a flaw to get two extra points and buy a level four skill/ability/talent that in play you would have to pay much more, then just fix it by paying two points that you will probably to get in the first session. My advice is if you're going to allow something like this then try to make it inconvenient in some way, something more difficult than just having to pay a few points and that's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T05:38:33-07:00","id":1521323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521276-removing-flaws?p=1521283#post1521283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Logically it makes sense for you to take some of these flaws, however I think it would be unbalanced to permit that, I mean, you can take a flaw to get two extra points and buy a level four skill/ability/talent that in play you would have to pay much more, then just fix it by paying two points that you will probably to get in the first session. My advice is if you're going to allow something like this then try to make it inconvenient in some way, something more difficult than just having to pay a few points and that's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand what you mean. What you mean by paying in the first session? Is there any rule for paying flaws?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T10:13:06-07:00","id":1521336,"title":"","content":"When you create the character sheet, after distributing the points you have 15 extra points to use wherever you want and you can use them to obtain qualities or gain more with failures, however if you do this exchange for later points it will be unbalanced. Here an example:<br /> <br /> &quot;Timmy wants his character to have five dexterity, but he needs 5 points to level up and he only has three, so he gets the flaw: Phobia and gains the two missing points. At the end of the first session, when the XP is distributed, Timmy decides he wants to use his points to cure his character's phobia, the ST approves and in the next session he is already without his handicap&quot;<br /> <br /> As I put in the example, Timmy managed to raise the dexterity, which would normally take 25P and got rid of the disadvantage just paying 2p that he got in the character's first session, basically a Hack. Did you understand?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T10:57:02-07:00","id":1521340,"title":"","content":"The freebie points to XP math is already horrifically imbalanced. Letting people get rid of Flaws isn't going to make it worse.<br /> <br /> The books have consistent stated that it can be done, but very inconsistently express how to do so mechanically.<br /> <br /> Most groups I've been in that have dealt with this have used one of two options, because esp. with Mages most Flaws can be removed with enough magic if no other option is available:<br /> <br /> Flat Flaw value x 3 (so a 3 point flaw costs 9 XP to remove).<br /> <br /> Current Flaw value x 3 (even if it isn't a scaled Flaw). So a 3 point Flaw would cost (9 + 6 + 3) 18 XP to fully remove.<br /> <br /> Both of these are inspired by the XP costs for Backgrounds, and the Revised Adversarial Backgrounds (which were just Flaws with a different name anyway).<br /> <br /> That said, I would seriously consider reducing a Flaws value if it is easily corrected, or has become more easily corrected since the Flaw was printed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T13:03:41-07:00","id":1521346,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27832_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27832\" data-vbnamecard=\"27832\">Psicose</a> <br /> <br /> I understand. However, where did you get that it costs 2 points of xp to remove a 2 dot flaw?<br /> <br /> And I'm also concerned about the in-game explanation. Why wouldn't someone be able to heal a physicsl flaw with Life magick? Or even by mundane means, like a surgery? <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521276-removing-flaws?p=1521340#post1521340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The freebie points to XP math is already horrifically imbalanced. Letting people get rid of Flaws isn't going to make it worse.<br /> <br /> The books have consistent stated that it can be done, but very inconsistently express how to do so mechanically.<br /> <br /> Most groups I've been in that have dealt with this have used one of two options, because esp. with Mages most Flaws can be removed with enough magic if no other option is available:<br /> <br /> Flat Flaw value x 3 (so a 3 point flaw costs 9 XP to remove).<br /> <br /> Current Flaw value x 3 (even if it isn't a scaled Flaw). So a 3 point Flaw would cost (9 + 6 + 3) 18 XP to fully remove.<br /> <br /> Both of these are inspired by the XP costs for Backgrounds, and the Revised Adversarial Backgrounds (which were just Flaws with a different name anyway).<br /> <br /> That said, I would seriously consider reducing a Flaws value if it is easily corrected, or has become more easily corrected since the Flaw was printed.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, there is no raw about that? The closest is the Adversarial bg and the cost of bg in xp?<br /> <br /> I don't think the second option makes much sense, but the first one does.<br /> <br /> But what about in-game. If a player wants to get rid of having myopia , through magick or not, how can we avoid that and should we?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T16:00:02-07:00","id":1521356,"title":"","content":"There are official suggestions in various books, but there's no RAW because buying off a Flaw with XP is essentially an optional rule to an optional rule and there was no simple RAW method printed.<br /> <br /> The second option is for people that are more concerned with Psicose's worries about trying to milk the system. It's hardly perfect, but it makes the costs of buying off Flaws closer in expense to the value they can provide if spent in a freebie-to-XP optimized fashion.<br /> <br /> And... I don't know what you mean about &quot;how can we avoid that.&quot; Depending on the cause of the myopia, treatment can be as simple as glasses, or expensive (and elective) surgery. If a character has myopia and wants to resolve it... that seems like a fine (if rather low stakes) goal. I don't see why you'd avoid it as a concept. The issue is more things like having a character (such as a mage starting with enough dots in Life to repair it) that doesn't have to do any work to justify removing the Flaw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T09:28:11-07:00","id":1521387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521276-removing-flaws?p=1521356#post1521356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are official suggestions in various books, but there's no RAW because buying off a Flaw with XP is essentially an optional rule to an optional rule and there was no simple RAW method printed.<br /> <br /> The second option is for people that are more concerned with Psicose's worries about trying to milk the system. It's hardly perfect, but it makes the costs of buying off Flaws closer in expense to the value they can provide if spent in a freebie-to-XP optimized fashion.<br /> <br /> And... I don't know what you mean about &quot;how can we avoid that.&quot; Depending on the cause of the myopia, treatment can be as simple as glasses, or expensive (and elective) surgery. If a character has myopia and wants to resolve it... that seems like a fine (if rather low stakes) goal. I don't see why you'd avoid it as a concept. The issue is more things like having a character (such as a mage starting with enough dots in Life to repair it) that doesn't have to do any work to justify removing the Flaw.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, doing something (magickal or not) would still cost XP ooc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T14:28:02-07:00","id":1521401,"title":"","content":"In the house rules I suggested? Yes.<br /> <br /> Some of the books would disagree, as some lean more towards treating Merits and Flaws like Backgrounds before XP for Backgrounds was introduced (that is: they are part of points for char-gen, but go up and down at ST discretion in play).<br /> <br /> For Mage specifically though, this is already kinda how things work. If you increase your Strength with Life, it's a short duration temporary effect so XP doesn't get involved, or a long term effect where you face issues like Permanent Paradox or Pattern Bleed... until you end the effect or buy Strength with XP.<br /> <br /> It's important to remember that XP is a metacurrency, not something that actually exists in the game-setting. The point of XP is to pace character advancement and some mixture of keeping characters roughly even in abilities while also rewarding certain actions over others (which means certain player can get ahead of others). From this perspective the in-game justification for why you're removing a Flaw isn't really what matters to how much XP it costs. After all, it doesn't matter to how much a physical Flaw gives you in freebies if it came from a birth defect, a severe injury, or a magical curse with a permanent effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T05:56:46-07:00","id":1521464,"title":"","content":"I would say removing a flaw requires dealing with the flaw in game. You can use magic to circumnavigate it, but I would think that would make the user subject to pattern bleed unless something was done to make the change permanent, and then may risk different flaws as a concequence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T05:57:48-07:00","id":1521465,"title":"","content":"To be clear, pattern bleed would be for removing physical/mental flaws, social or supernatural would require different means and may attract different problems in the attempt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T07:19:41-07:00","id":1521811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1521276-removing-flaws#post1521276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure there is any rule about that (couldn't find in M20, at least), but ia it possible to get rid of flaws?<br /> <br /> Do it costs xp?<br /> <br /> There are many physical and mental flaws, some wuite severe and other more light, like hard of seeing, which could be easily corrected with cirurgy.<br /> <br /> And what about magick? Life or Mind could easily heal many flaws. How do you rule that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1303543-experience-costs-of-merits-and-flaws-20th-anniversary\">asked the same once</a>. The only rules someone was able to provide were:<ul><li>DAV20 Corebook - pages 419 (merits/flaws cost as Background), 185 (Background point costs 2 x Current Rating in XP)</li> <li>M20 Corebook - p.253 (Background point costs 3 x Current Rating in XP)</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}